# Line endings and diffs. Rules from github.com/gitattributes/gitattributes
# (Common, Go), only for the files this repository has.

# LF on every platform: every file ends up on Linux, in an image or a
# host (Containerfile heredocs, scripts, sysroot configs), where a CR
# breaks bash, sudoers, sysctl and systemd. Git detects binaries.
*          text=auto eol=lf

# Hunk headers name the enclosing section or function: git's built-in
# diff drivers.
*.md       diff=markdown
*.go       diff=golang
*.sh       diff=bash

# Patches apply to upstream's files: kept byte for byte, CRs included.
*.patch    -text
